#import "../template.typ": somatic_page

// PHASE 4 - PAGE 24: FEAR & ANXIETY - PROMPTS
// Mirroring technique + Mad-lib structured prompts per Shadow Work Philosopher

#somatic_page(
  title: "Befriending Fear",
  body_text: [
    Place your hand on your belly or chest. Notice what happens when you ask yourself: *What am I afraid of?* Perhaps a flutter arises, or a familiar dread pools in your solar plexus. This sensation is fear's language. We are learning to listen.
    
    #v(0.5cm)
    
    #set text(style: "italic", size: 10.5pt)
    
    *1. Right now, my greatest fear is* __________.
    
    When I think about this fear, my body responds by __________ *(tightening, numbing, racing, freezing)*.
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))

    #v(0.8cm)
    *2. If my anxiety could speak, it would say:*
    
    "I am trying to protect you from __________."
    
    "I learned to watch for danger because __________."
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))

    #v(0.8cm)
    *3. If I were not afraid, I would* __________.
    
    The life I would be living is __________.
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))
    #v(1em)
    #line(length: 100%, stroke: (dash: "dotted"))

    #v(0.8cm)
    *4. To my fear, I want to say:* "__________."
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
